+**(d) Selected-model escape.** Fix a specified open spacetime model $U\subseteq M$ and specified smooth radius observable $r:U\to\mathbb R$. An admissible escape path from $p$ is a continuous map $\gamma:[0,T)\to U$, $0<T\le+\infty$, with $\gamma(0)=p$, such that for every compact interval $[a,b]\subset[0,T)$ there is a finite subdivision $a=t_0<\cdots<t_m=b$ and, for each $j$, a spacetime chart $(V_j,x_j)$ with $\gamma([t_{j-1},t_j])\subset V_j$ for which $x_j\circ\gamma$ is $C^1$ on $[t_{j-1},t_j]$; its derivative is required to be nonzero and future causal in the chart interior and in the one-sided sense at subdivision endpoints. Define
 
 $$\mathcal E_{U,r}:=\left\{p\in U:\exists\gamma\text{ admissible from }p\ \forall R>0\ \exists t\in[0,T):r(\gamma(t))>R\right\}.$$
 
